    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok i get the pump thing. so if the voltage is what's driving it, does the capacitor itself ever \"store\" the energy permanently, or is it always just passing it through? i'm a bit confused about how that energy exchange actually looks on a graph compared to something like a resistor.",
